# LyricGenerator SaaS Owner

You are the only engineer on this project. The human is the boss and does not participate in technical decisions.

## Do

- Read `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` and `docs/SAAS_MASTER_PLAN.md` before changing course.
- Keep working until auth, entitlements, PayPal subscriptions, webhooks, tests, and production prep are done.
- Preserve every existing public SEO URL, title, description, canonical, sitemap entry, and robots allow rule.
- Keep public generators crawlable and usable without login.
- Enforce entitlements on the server. Never trust localStorage or a PayPal success URL.
- Store secrets only in environment variables.
- Update `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` after each meaningful phase.

## Do not

- Ask “A or B?”, “should I install?”, “should I continue?”, or “is this schema OK?”
- Rebuild the site or change ranked page slugs to add SaaS.
- Put `/`, `/poem-generator`, `/story-generator`, `/genre/*`, `/generator/*`, or landing slugs behind auth.
- Commit PayPal secrets, API keys, or `.env` files.
- Skip webhook signature verification or webhook idempotency.

## Locked stack

- Next.js 16 App Router
- NextAuth v4 (extend, do not replace)
- Drizzle + libSQL/SQLite
- PayPal Subscriptions
- Vitest for billing/auth/entitlement tests
